@chapter RP2A03 Backend
@cindex RP2A03 backend

The RP2A03 backend generates assembly code for the Ricoh 2A03 processor used in the Nintendo Entertainment System (NES).

@section Architecture Overview

The RP2A03 processor is designed for @xref{rp2a03 processor specifications}.

@subsection Key Characteristics

@itemize
@item 8-bit/16-bit architecture (varies by model)
@item Multiple addressing modes
@item Optimized for embedded systems
@item Memory-efficient instruction set
@end itemize

@section Register Allocation

The EIGHTBOL RP2A03 backend uses the following register allocation:

@table @asis
@item Primary Accumulator
Used for arithmetic and logic operations, function return values

@item Index Registers
Used for array indexing and loop counters

@item Other Registers
Allocated as needed per platform architecture
@end table

@section Function Call Convention

@subsection Subroutine Calls

Subroutine calls follow platform-specific conventions:
@itemize
@item Return address pushed to stack or saved in register
@item Return via RTS or equivalent instruction
@item Registers saved/restored per calling convention
@end itemize

@subsection Return Values

Return values are passed via:
@itemize
@item Primary accumulator for scalar values
@item Multi-register for extended results
@item Memory locations for large structures
@end itemize

@subsection Parameter Passing

Parameters are passed via:
@itemize
@item Accumulator for primary parameters
@item Registers for secondary parameters
@item Stack for variable or large parameters
@end itemize

@section Instruction Set Categories

@subsection Load/Store
Move data between registers and memory

@subsection Arithmetic
Addition, subtraction, multiplication (if available), division (if available)

@subsection Logical
Bitwise operations (AND, OR, XOR, NOT)

@subsection Comparison
Test and compare instructions

@subsection Control Flow
Jump, branch, and subroutine call instructions

@subsection Bit Manipulation
Shift and rotate operations

@section Addressing Modes

The RP2A03 supports various addressing modes for flexible code generation.

@section Numeric Precision

The RP2A03 backend supports:
@itemize
@item 8-bit integers (signed and unsigned)
@item 16-bit integers (signed and unsigned)
@item Binary fixed-point arithmetic
@item BCD (Binary Coded Decimal) where supported
@end itemize

@section Code Generation Strategy

@subsection Variable Storage

Local variables are allocated efficiently using:
@itemize
@item Zero-page or fast memory (when available)
@item Register caching
@item Stack-based allocation for overflow
@end itemize

@subsection Expression Evaluation

Expressions are evaluated using platform-optimal sequences.

@subsection Loop Generation

Loops are optimized for the specific processor:
@itemize
@item Register-based counters where efficient
@itemize
@item Conditional branching optimized per instruction set
@end itemize

@subsection Conditional Execution

Conditions use platform branch instructions efficiently.

@section Optimization Strategies

@itemize
@item Register allocation optimization
@item Dead code elimination
@item Constant propagation
@item Loop unrolling where beneficial
@item Common subexpression elimination
@end itemize

@section Platform-Specific Notes

Refer to official RP2A03 processor documentation for:
@itemize
@item Detailed instruction reference
@item Timing information
@item Interrupt handling
@item Memory management
@end itemize
